{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.antitone_hypothesis_is_necessary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.antitone_hypothesis_is_necessary","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L247-L258","doc":"**Antitonicity is load-bearing, not decoration.**  Without it a single row below `lam` says\nnothing about the tail: take `Γ = (1, 2, 2, …)` and `lam = 1`.  Then `Γ 0 ≤ lam` holds and the\nrow-1 gradient is `+1`, so the tail is charged a positive amount and the certificate over the\npadded index set is strictly larger than the one over the used coordinates.\n\nStated as a refutation rather than a remark because a hypothesis nobody has shown to bite is\nindistinguishable from one that does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.padded_tail_charge_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.padded_tail_charge_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L230-L245","doc":"**The composition: an antitone tail is charged exactly nothing.**  `gradient_nonpos_of_antitone_tail`\nfeeds `box_charge_eq_zero_of_nonpos` directly, so every padded row past `J` contributes zero to\nthe certificate's linear term — not a bounded amount, zero.\n\nThis is the fact the bottom-edge measurement reports (`padded charge 0.0, tail 0.0 [exactly zero\n(g ≤ 0, lo = w = 0, Γ monotone)]`), and it is why `sum_charge_extend` rather than\n`sum_charge_extend_le` is the operative form there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.gradient_nonpos_of_antitone_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.gradient_nonpos_of_antitone_tail","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L207-L228","doc":"**The hypothesis `sum_charge_extend` assumes, discharged from monotonicity.**\n\n`sum_charge_extend` is stated over *\"if every padded coordinate is charged zero\"*, and says in\nits own docstring that the analytic content is elsewhere: *\"the padded coordinates satisfy\n`box_charge_eq_zero_of_nonpos`, and that is checked, not assumed.\"*  This is the lemma that\nstops it being assumed, for the one reason the bottom-edge frame actually supplies.\n\nThe per-row gradient is `Γ j - c j - lam`, with `Γ` the row's tangent slope, `c j ≥ 0` the linear\nwall cost, and `lam ≥ 0` the integrality-gap multiplier.  `Γ` is *antitone* in the row index, so\na single row `J` with `Γ J ≤ lam` forces the whole tail beyond it non-positive — one inequality\ncovers infinitely many coordinates, which is exactly what a certificate at every block length\nneeds.\n\nNote `c` enters only through `0 ≤ c j`: subtracting a non-negative cost can only help, so the\nbound does not depend on the wall's shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.capped_gt_is_sufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.capped_gt_is_sufficient","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L200-L205","doc":"The direction that *is* valid: a capped maximum is a lower bound on the true one, so a capped\nvalue EXCEEDING a bound does refute the bound.  Only the refuting direction survives. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.capped_lt_not_sufficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.capped_lt_not_sufficient","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L191-L198","doc":"**A capped maximum falling short proves nothing about the true one.**  `cap ≤ true` and\n`cap < other` are jointly satisfiable with `¬ (true ≤ other)`, so the inference is invalid.\n\nThis is the shape of the corpus's sole recorded evidence for `Xbot(s) ≤ Xblock(s)`: a bottom\ntable whose enumeration cap was saturated at the measured point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sum_charge_extend_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sum_charge_extend_le","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L174-L189","doc":"**The version the measurement actually needs.**  The padded coordinates are not free, so\nthey are *bounded* rather than deleted: whatever they are charged in total, the certificate over\nthe larger index set exceeds the one over `ι` by at most that.\n\nThis is the honest form of `sum_charge_extend`, and the two differ in exactly the way a\ngeometric tail differs from a vanishing one — which is the whole content of the bottom-edge\ncase, where every slope is strictly positive and only the *decay* is available. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sum_charge_extend","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sum_charge_extend","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L157-L172","doc":"**The same bound over a larger index set.**  Split the coordinates into the ones the ascent\npoint actually uses and the ones it was padded with; if every padded coordinate is charged zero,\nthe certificate's linear term is exactly the one computed over the used coordinates alone.\n\nThis is what turns a certificate at one block length into a certificate at every block length.\nIt is a statement about the *sum*, and it carries no analytic content — which is the point: the\nanalytic content is that the padded coordinates satisfy `box_charge_eq_zero_of_nonpos`, and that\nis checked, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.box_charge_eq_zero_of_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.box_charge_eq_zero_of_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L141-L155","doc":"**Padding a certificate is free.**  A coordinate whose gradient is non-positive and whose\nreference point sits ON the lower box endpoint is charged exactly nothing — in *either* branch\nof the sign split, which is why the hypothesis is `g ≤ 0` and not `g < 0`.\n\n`boundary_charge_eq_zero` above is the strict case seen at a KKT-active coordinate.  This is the\none the length argument needs, because a padded coordinate may have gradient exactly `0`, and\nthere the `if` takes the *other* branch (`0 ≤ g`) and lands on `g * (hi - w)` — zero for a\ndifferent reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sup_le_of_supergradient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.sup_le_of_supergradient","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L121-L139","doc":"**The certificate.**  If `F` obeys a supergradient inequality at `w`, and every `u` that\nreaches the incumbent `V` is confined to the box `∏ [lo i, hi i]`, then `F` is bounded above\neverywhere by an explicit number: the incumbent, or `F w` plus the box-maximised linear term.\n\nNeither hypothesis mentions concavity by name — `hconc` is what concavity *supplies*, and\n`hbox` is what an independent coercivity bound supplies.  The conclusion holds at every `u`,\nincluding those outside the box, which is the point: outside it, `F u < V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.abs_charge_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.abs_charge_pos","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L113-L119","doc":"The absolute-value charge at the same point is strictly positive — so the two differ by the\nwhole of it, not by a refinement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.boundary_charge_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.boundary_charge_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L106-L111","doc":"**Why the case split is worth `2.25e11`.**  A coordinate pinned to the lower boundary\n(`w = lo`) with a strictly negative gradient contributes **exactly nothing** to the slack. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.box_mul_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SupergradientCertificate.box_mul_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SupergradientCertificate.lean#L94-L104","doc":"**The box maximisation.**  Over `x ∈ [lo, hi]`, the linear term `g * (x - w)` is largest at\n`hi` when `g` is non-negative and at `lo` when it is negative.\n\nThis is the load-bearing case split of the certificate.  Both branches are needed: replacing the\n`g < 0` branch by anything that does not evaluate at `lo` gives a valid but far weaker bound. ","signatureChunk":0}]}